# META-PREFIX-DECODE over a running turn. The fake gateway holds each answer
# after six chunks (`held`), so a turn is running for the keys below it.
# (a) `ESC ESC [ A`: fx's meta-prefixed Up, a paragraph move
# (escape_parser.zig:552-555, :561-568, :83-89@481104fd), and no Escape: the
# turn runs on, nothing is armed, nothing is recalled. (b) Two Escape bytes
# in one burst: two Escapes, as fx's theme monitor delivers them
# (theme_monitor.zig:82-93, :150-164; app_bootstrap_runtime.zig:481-483): the
# first arms the interrupt and the second stops the turn
# (app_input_runtime.zig:2740-2758). (c) The next turn, and a person's two
# presses 0.3 s apart: the second stops it.
gateway p5-cancel-double-escape-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
type stream please
wait 1
key Enter
held
wait 1
snap mid
key -H 1b 1b 5b 41
wait 0.6
snap a-meta-up
key Escape Escape
wait 1.5
snap b-burst-cancelled
release
wait 1
type stream again
wait 1
key Enter
held
wait 1
snap mid2
key Escape
wait 0.3
key Escape
wait 2
snap c-person-cancelled
release
wait 1
gwlog
